# SA-CCR netting-set membership — intensional rules (Datalog Horn clauses in N3).
# TC-MEGA-FIBO-01 lane L38. STRATIFICATION LAYER 1.
# Positive Horn clauses only: no negation in this layer. Every clause is
# range-restricted (every variable in the head appears in the body), so the
# least Herbrand model exists and forward-chaining saturates finitely over the
# extensional layer-0 facts. Boundedness: heads introduce only reg: terms
# already named in the body; no value invention, no recursion beyond the
# linear, well-founded nettingSetOf chain.

# NAMESPACE RECONCILIATION (WO-13 decision): reg:
# (<http://graphlaw.org/ns/mega/fibo/reg#>) is a first-class scenario-local
# namespace of this self-contained mega ontology; it is not mapped onto or
# renamed under repo-canonical surfaces (ontologies/sql-ast.ttl,
# ggen/sql-dialect/). log: is the standard CWM/swap vocabulary. Full per-term
# decisions: README.md, "Vocabulary grounding and RECONCILIATION-REQUIRED".

@prefix reg: <http://graphlaw.org/ns/mega/fibo/reg#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R1.1  Two cleared trades belong to the same netting set if they share
#       a netting agreement and are in the same CCP membership.
{ ?t1 a reg:Trade . ?t1 reg:nettingAgreement ?na .
  ?t2 a reg:Trade . ?t2 reg:nettingAgreement ?na .
  ?t1 reg:nettingSetOf ?ns . ?t2 reg:nettingSetOf ?ns . }
=> { ?t1 reg:coNettedWith ?t2 . ?t2 reg:coNettedWith ?t1 . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R1.2  A trade nets into the netting set of its holder's clearing
#       membership when the agreement is SA-CCR eligible.
{ ?t a reg:Trade ;
     reg:holder ?h ;
     reg:nettingAgreement ?na .
  ?na a reg:SACCREligibleAgreement .
  ?h reg:ccpMemberOf ?ccp .
  ?ns reg:nettingSetForCCP ?ccp ;
      reg:governingJurisdiction ?j .
  ?na reg:governingJurisdiction ?j . }
=> { ?t reg:nettingSetOf ?ns . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R1.3  A netting set exists for a legal entity holding an ISDA margin
#       agreement with a threshold in its jurisdiction's cap band.
{ ?h a reg:LEIHolder ;
     reg:nettingSetRef ?nsRef ;
     reg:jurisdiction ?j .
  ?ma a reg:MarginAgreement ;
     reg:party ?h ;
     reg:marginThreshold ?thr .
  ?ns reg:nettingSetFor ?nsRef . }
=> { ?ns reg:nettingSetMember ?h .
     ?ns reg:nettingSetJurisdiction ?j . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R1.4  Transitive co-netting closure within one set (bounded: only over
#       pairs already co-netted by R1.1, scoped by the nettingSetOf guard).
{ ?t1 reg:coNettedWith ?t2 . ?t2 reg:coNettedWith ?t3 .
  ?t1 reg:nettingSetOf ?ns . }
=> { ?t1 reg:coNettedWith ?t3 . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R1.5  A netting set is SA-CCR recognized when every member holds a
#       valid LEI node and a margin agreement in the set's jurisdiction.
{ ?ns reg:nettingSetMember ?h .
  ?h reg:leiCode ?lei .
  ?ma reg:party ?h ;
      reg:governingJurisdiction ?j .
  ?ns reg:nettingSetJurisdiction ?j . }
=> { ?ns a reg:SACCRRecognizedNettingSet . } .
